IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`

-- 26 U.S.C. section 121. LAYER 1, module 8: subsections (e), (f) and (g).
-- Section 877(a)(1), section 1034 and section 1223(6) are not among the sources; section 1034 is repealed and section 1223(6) is repealed too (the notes say so; context only).
-- The facts that depend on them are asked, not worked out.

§ `Subsection (e): denial of exclusion for expatriates`

-- src:151 | (e) Denial of exclusion for expatriates
-- src:152 | This section shall not apply to any sale or exchange by an individual if the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1) applies to such individual.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(e) (src:151-152)
GIVEN `the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1) applies to the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(e) this section applies to the sale or exchange by the individual` MEANS
    IF `the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1) applies to the individual`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section shall not apply to any sale or exchange by an individual if the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1) applies to such individual." (a flat negative)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is limited by "if the treatment provided by section 877(a)(1) applies"; outside it the text is silent.
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Subsection (f): election to have section not apply`

-- src:153 | (f) Election to have section not apply
-- src:154 | This section shall not apply to any sale or exchange with respect to which the taxpayer elects not to have this section apply.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(f) (src:153-154)
GIVEN `the taxpayer elects not to have this section apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(f) this section applies to the sale or exchange` MEANS
    IF `the taxpayer elects not to have this section apply`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section shall not apply to any sale or exchange with respect to which the taxpayer elects not to have this section apply." (a flat negative)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is limited to a sale "with respect to which the taxpayer elects not to have this section apply"; outside it the text is silent.
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Subsection (g): residences acquired in rollovers under section 1034`

-- The aggregate periods are given as a number of days, which the caller adds to the days owned and used.
-- Whether those days must lie inside the 5-year period is not said; they are added as stated (fork F15).
-- src:156 | For purposes of this section, in the case of property the acquisition of which by the taxpayer resulted under section 1034 [^1] (as in effect on the day before the date of the enactment of this section) in the nonrecognition of any part of the gain realized on the sale or exchange of another residence, in determining the period for which the taxpayer has owned and used such property as the taxpayer’s principal residence, there shall be included the aggregate periods for which such other residence (and each prior residence taken into account under section 1223(6) [^1] in determining the holding period of such property) had been so owned and used.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(g) (src:156)
GIVEN `the acquisition of the property resulted under section 1034 in the nonrecognition of part of the gain on another residence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate days the other residence and each prior residence had been owned and used as the principal residence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 121(g) the days the other residence was owned and used are included` MEANS
    IF `the acquisition of the property resulted under section 1034 in the nonrecognition of part of the gain on another residence`
    THEN JUST `the aggregate days the other residence and each prior residence had been owned and used as the principal residence`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of property the acquisition of which by the taxpayer resulted under section 1034 (as in effect on the day before the date of the enactment of this section) in the nonrecognition of any part of the gain realized on the sale or exchange of another residence" (section 1034 is repealed and outside the sources)
    ELSE NOTHING
